; USBECM.EXE's description, for cargo drivers: it goes into the zip as
; USBECM.INF (with Source= added) and into CATALOG.TXT as one line per
; [Devices] entry. Raise Version= for every change that is published.
; The kernel's built-in CDC Ethernet driver took every USB adapter with an
; ECM configuration, whatever its IDs; this driver replaces it (D-259), so
; its one line is the class: any vendor, any product, an interface of
; class 02h subclass 06h (communications, Ethernet Control Model).
[Driver]
Name=USBECM
Version=1.0.0-1
File=USBECM.EXE
Description=USB Ethernet adapter (CDC ECM)
Licence=MIT
Basic=Yes

[Devices]
USB:*:* cdc-ecm
